"cues": [
{
"block": "b1",
"t": 3.2,
"end": 7.496,
"text": "Here is the whole machine, from start to finish, on one question."
},
{
"block": "b1",
"t": 7.856,
"end": 14.671,
"text": "Emma asks: how many city e-bike battery packs do we have in Manchester stores?"
},
{
"block": "b2",
"t": 15.271,
"end": 23.758,
"text": "The app wraps her words in a chat: its own instructions, her question, and a header that says the assistant speaks next."
},
{
"block": "b2",
"t": 24.164,
"end": 29.389,
"text": "The tokenizer cuts all of it into 100 tiles, each with its own number."
},
{
"block": "b2",
"t": 29.865,
"end": 31.943,
"text": "The date is cut digit by digit."
},
{
"block": "b2",
"t": 32.303,
"end": 37.748,
"text": "Manchester is a single tile, number 19361."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 38.748,
"end": 41.825,
"text": "Each tile looks up its row in the embedding table."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 42.231,
"end": 49.383,
"text": "The table has 151,936 rows, one for every token the model knows."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 49.789,
"end": 52.68,
"text": "Each row is 896 numbers."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 53.039,
"end": 58.67,
"text": "So every tile now stands with a column of 896 numbers behind it."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 59.67,
"end": 62.027,
"text": "The 100 columns enter block 1."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 62.503,
"end": 64.001,
"text": "First, attention."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 64.558,
"end": 68.842,
"text": "Each position makes a query, a key and a value."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 69.248,
"end": 76.319,
"text": "Its query meets the keys of the earlier positions, never the later ones, and the values of the best matches flow in."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 76.679,
"end": 80.847,
"text": "Then the MLP reworks each column on its own."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 81.847,
"end": 87.188,
"text": "Attention is not one look, but fourteen, side by side: the heads."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 87.547,
"end": 89.823,
"text": "Each head looks in its own way."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 90.473,
"end": 95.941,
"text": "In block 24, head 2 puts 65 percent of its weight on Manchester."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 96.487,
"end": 102.234,
"text": "In block 12, head 13 rests all of its weight on the very first token."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 103.234,
"end": 110.572,
"text": "Every block updates all 100 columns, not just the last one, all the way through 24 blocks."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 110.978,
"end": 117.805,
"text": "The other columns matter: at every block, they hold the keys and values the last column reads."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 118.107,
"end": 130.169,
"text": "The stack holds 494,032,768 learnt numbers, every one set in training, as we saw in section 8."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 131.169,
"end": 133.688,
"text": "At the top, only the last column speaks."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 134.048,
"end": 142.28,
"text": "It is scored against every row of the same table, all 151,936."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 142.756,
"end": 145.902,
"text": "Softmax turns the scores into probabilities."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 146.262,
"end": 148.271,
"text": "We: 56 percent."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 148.63,
"end": 149.908,
"text": "As: 8."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 150.314,
"end": 151.963,
"text": "Manchester: 6."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 152.369,
"end": 154.343,
"text": "We is chosen."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 155.343,
"end": 158.373,
"text": "We joins the row, and the machine runs again."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 159.023,
"end": 161.717,
"text": "But the 100 earlier columns are not run again."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 162.123,
"end": 165.85,
"text": "Their keys and values were kept, in the KV cache."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 166.5,
"end": 174.429,
"text": "So each new token sends just one new column through the 24 blocks, and that column still reads every position before it."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 174.987,
"end": 175.683,
"text": "Currently."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 175.881,
"end": 176.38,
"text": "Have."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 176.6,
"end": 177.727,
"text": "A space."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 178.727,
"end": 179.575,
"text": "Then the number."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 180.039,
"end": 182.082,
"text": "One, at 34 percent."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 182.547,
"end": 183.15,
"text": "Zero."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 183.545,
"end": 184.219,
"text": "Zero."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 184.671,
"end": 192.903,
"text": "Token by token, the answer grows: We currently have 100 city e-bike battery packs available in our Manchester stores."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 193.251,
"end": 196.467,
"text": "Then the end-of-turn token, and the loop stops."
},
{
"block": "b10",
"t": 197.467,
"end": 200.323,
"text": "Every step ran exactly as it was built to."
},
{
"block": "b10",
"t": 200.973,
"end": 201.879,
"text": "Nothing broke."
},
{
"block": "b10",
"t": 202.436,
"end": 205.71,
"text": "And still, the answer is 100."
},
{
"block": "b10",
"t": 206.186,
"end": 210.9,
"text": "Ledgerline, Northbridge's own record, says 5,400."
},
{
"block": "b10",
"t": 211.457,
"end": 215.3,
"text": "So why did a machine that worked perfectly make this number up?"
}
]
}